comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-21T05:07:15.543Z","harness:claude-code","A fourth deferred case from Codex review round 6 of the same change, on 2026-11-21. Two clones repair the same out-of-band edit independently, giving equivalent bridges A and B. They merge in both directions (one result keeps A plus a neutral copy of B, the other B plus a neutral copy of A), each then records an ordinary update, and the two results are merged. The union retains repair order A then B on one side and B then A on the other, and the later updates keep the equivalent-bridge path from applying, so the merge driver refuses with \"History union cannot preserve contradictory original branch event orders\". It fails closed and loses nothing: the file stays unresolved for manual recovery. A fix normalizes a run of equivalent repairs (live or neutral) before ordering the later edits, keeping one live bridge and neutral copies for the other repairs' provenance.\n"
  "2026-11-21T06:03:32.147Z","harness:claude-code","The fourth deferred case (reciprocal equivalent-repair merges followed by ordinary updates on both sides) is fixed on PR #1762 in commit 0db4719f8, prompted by a CodeRabbit finding on the closeout head. Before ordering, mergeHistoryStreams turns both sides' runs of the same repair into one shared run: ours, plus neutral copies of theirs' repairs ours lacks. Only the later records are then ordered. The regression case lives in the history-bridge integration spec. This item keeps the other three: history-diff before-values for inexact versions, epoch-2 variant duplicate evidence, and holding the closer to the proven epoch and variant."
  "2026-11-21T10:14:21.155Z","harness:claude-code","Two further deferred cases from CodeRabbit's full review of b71d8fb74 on PR #1762. (1) Redaction accepts a bridge whose segment digest matches even when its own patch was resealed to a different one, since the digest covers the records before the bridge and not the bridge's effect. A redaction could then dissolve it and write the replayed state back. This needs a hand-resealed bridge record. The fix is for redaction to require that the closer's patch reproduces its recorded after_hash. (2) Two clones that repair one break in the same millisecond, with the same author and message but different agent_instance provenance, share one record identity, so the merge reports identical and keeps one repair's provenance. The fix derives bridge identity from stable original-repair provenance, while a neutral copy and a marker-only reseal still match their original."
body: ""
